# xtdl-values-example: a FICTIONAL format, invented only for this example: a
# 23-byte binary report that shows the value transforms of engine-spec 0.15
# (octal digits, sign and magnitude, an integer scale, a 6-bit character set
# and a scaled IEEE float). Layout: pack.md.
format        xtdl-values-example
version       0.1.0
distribution  controlled
source        "invented for this example; no external document"
uses          xtdl
wire          bits
word_bytes    1
bit_order     msb

field  uid        0:0:15     octal
field  lat        0:15:25    smscale:1/100000
field  lon        0:40:26    smscale:1/100000
field  time_ms    0:66:32    uiscale:1000
field  callsign   0:98:54    chars:icao6
field  speed_ms   0:152:32   f32scale:1/10
